<!-- <hr> -->

<p>An experiment I tried recently with ChatGPT was to see if it could generate some Podcast suggestions for me based on my current podcast subscriptions. I was able to supply ChatGPT with an <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OPML">OPML file</a> that is commonly used to transfer podcast subscriptions between podcast apps.</p>
<p>Below is the conversation I had:</p>
<p>🧑‍💻</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Are you aware of the OPML.xml format?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>🤖</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Yes, I'm aware of the OPML (Outline Processor Markup Language) format. OPML is an XML-based file format used for creating outlines of information. It's commonly used for exchanging lists of web feeds between web feed aggregators or between feed aggregators and podcasting clients. OPML files typically contain a hierarchical structure of outlines, which can include links, metadata, and other information. It's a simple and widely adopted format for organizing and sharing structured data.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>🧑‍💻</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I have an OPML podcast file with my current podcasts, can you analyze the text and recommend some other podcasts I might be interested based on my current subscriptions?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>🤖</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Sure, please provide me with the OPML file, and I'll be happy to help analyze it and suggest some other podcasts based on your current subscriptions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>🧑‍💻</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8' standalone='yes' ?&gt;
